// KSI social-service codes to ICF mappings, codes VA1-VA
// Several sources map to the same target; each mapping is its own assertion.
context {
 collection "ksi-icf" version="2026.1"
 source system="KSI" release="2026"
 target system="ICF"
}
defaults {
 mappings {
 preference "primary"
 assessment-method "source-default-granularity"
 }
}
mapping "VA1.1" source="VA1" target="d298A" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target effect=omitted quality=60 {
 confidence 2 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence-unassessable@1"
 comment "en" """
 Source VA1 = the KSI section for behaviors and habits (general): the topic
 parent of all VA1.* activities (assessment, counseling, support, training regarding
 behaviors/habits). Target ICF d298A (Handling one's behavior) is the
 corpus's established behavior-management anchor (committed precedent: SDK section 'Att hantera
 sitt beteende' and all SDK.* children map to d298A). Why this target: d298A is the only ICF
 d-code directly denoting behavior handling, and the KSI<->ICF crosswalk convention is a
 topic-collapse (the activity subject maps to the ICF activity/participation d-code). Why broader
 (low): low tier — VA1 explicitly covers BOTH (behaviors, covered by d298A) AND
 (habits, closer to d230 the imported designation), so d298A subsumes the behavior axis
 but leaves the habits axis uncovered; the target is the best available standard concept with a
 real, well-understood breadth gap, not independently crosswalked for this section. Athena-local
 ICF mirror; no web.
 """ suspect=quoted-text
}
mapping "VA1.AA.ZZ.1" source="VA1.AA.ZZ" target="d298A" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
 confidence 2 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence-unassessable@1"
 comment "en" """
 Source VA1.AA.ZZ = Assessment of behaviors and habits;
 one of the VA1 activity-type children (assessment / observation / conversation / training /
 support modality) about the behaviors-and-habits topic. Target ICF d298A
 (Handling one's behavior) is the corpus's established behavior anchor (precedent: SDK.* ->
 d298A). Why this target: the KSI<->ICF crosswalk convention is a topic-collapse - the activity
 subject (behaviors/habits) maps to the ICF activity/participation d-code, and the activity-type
 modifier (AA=assessment, AM=observation, AS/PU/PV=conversation, etc.) does not change the ICF
 topic target (corpus precedent: SA1.AA/AM/AS/PU/RC all -> d110-d199). ICF has no per-modality
 assessment-vs-counseling split for behavior. Why broader (low): low tier - d298A subsumes the
 behavior axis but VA1's topic also includes (habits, closer to d230 daily routine),
 which d298A leaves uncovered; best available standard concept with a real breadth gap, not
 independently crosswalked for this code. Athena-local ICF mirror; no web.
 """ suspect=quoted-text
}
