mapping "VA2.1" source="VA2" target="d298A" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
 confidence 2 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence-unassessable@1"
 comment "en" """
 Source VA2 = the KSI
 section for behaviors/habits regarding alcohol, narcotics, tobacco, doping
 (performance-enhancing drugs), and gambling - the substance-use and addictive-behavior cluster.
 ICF has NO addiction/substance-specific d-code (verified: no ICF row for
 beroende/missbruk/alkohol/narkotik/spel). Two defensible standard anchors: (1) d298A (Handling one's behavior) - the corpus's established behavior anchor (SDK ->
 d298A), which subsumes the behavior-management axis of substance-use behavior; (2) d570 (Looking after one's health) - the ICF health-behavior/maintenance concept, directly
 relevant because substance-use behaviors are health-risk behaviors. Why these targets: no single
 ICF code captures addictive behavior, so the behavior axis (d298A, primary, broader - VA2's
 substance scope is a subset of all behavior handling) and the health-behavior axis (d570,
 related - substance use is associated with health maintenance, not equivalent to it) are both
 recorded. Why broader + related: low/weak tiers - d298A is the best primary with a breadth gap,
 d570 is a weaker aspect-level lead. Athena-local ICF mirror; no web.
 """ suspect=quoted-text
}
mapping "VA2.2" source="VA2" target="d570" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
 confidence 2 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence-unassessable@1"
}
mapping "VA2.AA.ZZ.1" source="VA2.AA.ZZ" target="d298A" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
 confidence 2 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence-unassessable@1"
 comment "en" """
 Source VA2.AA.ZZ = Assessment of substance/gambling behaviors; one of the VA2 activity-type
 children (assessment / manual-based test / observation / conversation) about the substance-use
 and gambling behavior topic. ICF has NO addiction-specific d-code. Two defensible anchors (same
 as the VA2 parent): (1) d298A (Handling one's behavior) - the
 established behavior anchor (SDK -> d298A), broader than the substance scope; (2) d570 (Looking after one's health) - the health-behavior axis, associated with
 substance-use risk. Why these targets: KSI<->ICF topic-collapse convention (activity-type
 modifier does not change the ICF topic; cf SA1.* -> d110-d199), and the substance-behavior topic
 has no single dedicated ICF code. Why broader + related: d298A is the best primary with a
 breadth gap; d570 is a weaker aspect-level lead (substance use is associated with, not
 equivalent to, health maintenance). Athena-local ICF mirror; no web.
 """ suspect=quoted-text
}
mapping "VA2.AA.ZZ.2" source="VA2.AA.ZZ" target="d570" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
