mapping "VA2.AC.ZZ.1" source="VA2.AC.ZZ" target="d298A" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
 confidence 2 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence-unassessable@1"
 comment "en" """
 Source VA2.AC.ZZ = Manual-based test or conversation about substance/gambling
 behaviors; one of the VA2 activity-type children (assessment / manual-based test / observation /
 conversation) about the substance-use and gambling behavior topic. ICF has NO addiction-specific
 d-code. Two defensible anchors (same as the VA2 parent): (1) d298A the behavior-management d-code
 (Handling one's behavior) - the established behavior anchor (SDK -> d298A), broader than the
 substance scope; (2) d570 (Looking after one's health) - the health-behavior
 axis, associated with substance-use risk. Why these targets: KSI<->ICF topic-collapse convention
 (activity-type modifier does not change the ICF topic; cf SA1.* -> d110-d199), and the
 substance-behavior topic has no single dedicated ICF code. Why broader + related: d298A is the
 best primary with a breadth gap; d570 is a weaker aspect-level lead (substance use is associated
 with, not equivalent to, health maintenance). Athena-local ICF mirror; no web.
 """ suspect=quoted-text
}
mapping "VA2.AC.ZZ.2" source="VA2.AC.ZZ" target="d570" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
